Description:
Annie Wright Schools seek an Institutional Analytics Coordinator to begin immediately. This is an exempt, full-time salaried position that reports to the Assistant Head of Schools. 




Mission Statement

Annie Wright’s strong community cultivates individual learners to become well-educated, creative, and responsible citizens for a global society.




About AWS

Tradition meets innovation at Annie Wright Schools, where we honor our rich history and traditions, embrace the present, and continue always to move forward. Founded in 1884, Annie Wright Schools serve students from age three through high school. The Lower and Middle Schools offer co-ed programs in Preschool through Grade 8, while separate Upper Schools for boys and girls offer day and boarding options in Grades 9 through 12, welcoming students from Tacoma and around the world. We are proud to be an International Baccalaureate World School, delivering IB programs in every division.




Position Description




Every student has a story, and every dataset tells part of that story. The Institutional Analytics Coordinator plays a critical role in helping Annie Wright Schools understand the experiences, outcomes, and opportunities of our students through thoughtful analysis of data, including academic, demographic, participatory, disciplinary, and self-reported outcomes. Working closely with the Assistant Head of Schools, Senior Leadership Team, and colleagues across the institution, the Institutional Analytics Coordinator transforms information into actionable insights that support student results, strengthen institutional effectiveness, and guide strategic decision-making. The Institutional Analytics Coordinator develops and maintains dashboards, reports, visualizations, forecasts, and analytical models that help school leaders better understand trends, evaluate programs, measure progress toward strategic goals, and identify opportunities to improve student outcomes and access to an Annie Wright education. In partnership with the Assistant Head of Schools, the Admissions team and the Business Office, the Institutional Analytics Coordinator also supports administration of the school's financial aid program through award modeling, budget forecasting, demographic and enrollment analysis, and reporting that helps guide access, affordability, and long-term financial aid strategy.




The Institutional Analytics Coordinator is a self-driven, curious, and creative professional who enjoys asking meaningful questions, exploring complex datasets, and uncovering patterns that might otherwise go unnoticed. The Institutional Analytics Coordinator goes beyond the technical and enjoys spending time exploring data and identifying interesting trends and insights. They are equally comfortable working independently on detailed analysis and collaborating with colleagues to solve institutional challenges. An engaged, ethical, and resourceful professional, the Institutional Analytics Coordinator possesses the communication, presentation, project management, and organizational skills necessary to translate complex information into clear and compelling narratives for a variety of audiences. By helping the school better understand who our students are, how they are experiencing Annie Wright, and how financial aid resources can best support the mission, this role contributes directly to the growth, health, and success of both our students and our broader community.




Core Job Responsibilities:

The Institutional Analytics Coordinator is responsible for:

Analyzing and interpreting student academic, behavioral, participation, wellness, assessment, and demographic data to identify trends and actionable insights;
Supporting the school's Student Thrivability Measure, institutional dashboards, recurring reports, and strategic metrics;
Conducting research and analysis that informs decision-making by school leadership, committees, and the Board of Trustees;
Developing visualizations, reports, and presentations that translate complex information into meaningful recommendations;
Analyzing assessment results and longitudinal student outcomes across cohorts and demographic groups;
Supporting administration of the school's financial aid program, including data analysis, award modeling, budget forecasting, and reporting;
Partnering with leaders across Divisions, enrollment, and finance, to answer strategic questions through data;
Promoting data quality, integrity, and effective use of institutional information systems;
Identifying opportunities to improve processes, reporting capabilities, and organizational decision-making through data.




Qualifications

The Institutional Analytics Coordinator will demonstrate key elements of the listed expertise and experiences. This is an aspirational list, and Annie Wright Schools encourages candidates to apply who may not currently possess, but are working on building, all of these qualities. The Institutional Analytics Coordinator:

holds a Bachelor of Arts or Science in data science, computer science, mathematics or a similar degree; 
has 2-5 years of experience in financial aid, enrollment management, or research, ideally within an independent school setting; experience with Blackbaud data and/or Clarity preferred;
has experience creating digestible data visualizations and communicating results to non-technical stakeholders; 
is proficient in Excel and Google Sheets; comfort with Python, R, or similar coding language to perform statistical analysis is preferred;
has expertise and experience with PowerBI;
Is able to collect, organize, and store data from disparate sources in Azure databases for long-term data organization and access;
possesses exceptional judgment and discretion in handling confidential financial information;
has a willingness to dig deeper and understand processes that create data; 
is highly organized and capable of developing and executing efficient workflow systems;
collaborates effectively across departments and stakeholders;
manages a fast-paced, dynamic work environment with flexibility, humor, and a focus on collaborative, team-based problem solving;
practices cultural humility in personal interactions;
is eligible to work in the United States. Note: Under our current employment policies, we are unable to sponsor work visas and do not offer positions to candidates who are not yet eligible to work in the United States.




Physical Requirements

Must be able to sit and stand for extended periods of time;
Must be able to lift at least 25 lbs;
Must be able to communicate and exchange information with others.




Salary & Benefits

This full-time, benefited position offers a salary range of $85,000-$105,000, depending on qualifications and experience. Benefits include the following, subject to the terms of the applicable benefit plan:

Medical, dental, and vision insurance
Employee Assistance Program
Life insurance
Accidental death & dismemberment insurance
Long-term disability insurance
Paid sick leave (known as Wellness Days): Each regular full-time employee earns 80 hours of Wellness leave per accrual year and prorated on a part-time basis
Eighteen (18) paid Holidays anticipated in 2026 
Tuition remission in accordance with school policy based on FTE. All fees and incidental expenses are the sole responsibility of the employee-parent
All children of benefited employees of AWS, who are currently enrolled at AWS, are eligible for extended day services at no charge when school is in session. Charges apply for faculty in-service days or similar days  
A 403(b) retirement plan with a 6% company match with a 3% employee contribution




Application Process

Annie Wright Schools remain firmly committed to a policy of equal employment opportunity. Annie Wright shall hire, promote, transfer, terminate, and make all other employment-related decisions without regard to an employee’s race, color, creed, sex, religion, age, national origin, marital status, sexual orientation, political ideology, the presence of any sensory, mental, or physical disability, or any other basis prohibited by law. Annie Wright Schools are actively seeking to create a more culturally diverse school community, and accordingly, applicants of color and underrepresented backgrounds are encouraged to apply. 




To apply, email a cover letter, resume, email and telephone contact information for 3-5 professional references, and this completed and signed application, all in PDF format, to Ms. Erin Gann, Executive Assistant to the Head of Schools, at erin_gann@aw.org. In accordance with Annie Wright Schools’ strategic focus on issues related to social justice, candidates should anticipate being asked to address how their past work, as well as future contributions, might serve to advance Annie Wright’s commitment to a more diverse and inclusive community. Applications for this position will be accepted until filled.

